  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: W extremity of Epipolai</p>\r\n<p>The fortress was first built by Dionysius I between 402 and 397 B.C. Various future modifications took place under Agathocles and Hiero II. The fortress remained in use following the Roman conquest of 212 B.C., continuing up to the Byzantine period.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A fortress built by Dionysius the Elder 9 km west of Syracuse, in the modern hamlet of Belvedere (Sicily).",
